VERDICT LOGIC
  part 1 says what a handoff really costs; part 2 says how much of the
  published 2.17 us was a memset; part 4 says whether fewer barriers are
  cheaper; part 5 says whether there is ANY stage size where a persistent
  kernel beats a graph.  If part 5 shows a crossover, the megakernel is
  not refuted -- it is simply not applicable at batch 1's large stages.
